    "summary": "Restored rubbings-theft-001's snapshot (a9b0961) except features/; `git diff --stat` against it was empty before any edit, and every path it touched is owned. Finding 1: each player's status now carries settledChoice and choiceDeadline (schema, MatchRoom notices, MatchView, HeadlessClient). A new purse-choice line says 'You chose X' / 'They chose X' / 'Taken by default: X', with the server's settled-at and deadline ticks as data attributes. Key and click handling is extracted into the pure chosenTheftType (hud.ts), and main.ts uses it. Web unit tests cover choiceLine plus key 1, key 2, clicks on options 1 and 2, and inputs that pick nothing. A new integration test runs through the real room: the guest holds both types, the host neither, and the host sends choose-theft for the type defaultTheftType would not take; the test checks settlement.choice === 'winner' and that the type moved. The default-deadline test now also asserts settledChoice 'default'. theft-loop now clicks '1: Moon' and asserts the host sees 'You chose Moon' (never 'Taken by default'), the guest sees 'They chose Moon', and deadline - settledAt >= 60 server ticks on both pages. I also added an untagged Playwright test that clicks the second of two options (the non-default Moon). Finding 2: a new expectRoomChecks helper (tracker uses it too) runs after every test in match, visibility and admission. 'removes a ship when its player leaves' also asserts the ledger player is 'left' and the room checks are clean. This surfaced a real bug: a join refused in onJoin still reached onDrop/onLeave and made the ledger refuse disconnectPlayer and quitPlayer for an unknown player. Both hooks now skip sessions the room never admitted. Finding 3: MatchTuning.random is a test-only seam (default cryptoRandom = node:crypto randomInt) and now supplies the world, ledger and duel seeds. New tests/integration/ledgerSeed.test.ts (source layout off) checks two seeds deal differently via createMatchLedger, then shows two matches with different codes and the same source get the same deal, and another source changes the deal. New apps/server/src/random.test.ts mocks node:crypto and shows the default source calls randomInt(0, 2**32) with sourceLayout off. Docs: architecture.md and README. Checks run from a fresh npm ci: typecheck ok; unit 905/905; integration 75/75 in 127 s (vitest 126 s; the sequential harness group is ~65 s of it); build ok. Browser: 9/9 passed (8 scenarios + 1 untagged) in 251 s, and check-report passed on that JSON report.",
